    "metaTitle": "Inverted Duty Structure Refund | FileFast",
    "metaDescription": "A document-led approach to reviewing a potential refund where input tax rates and output tax rates differ. Practical records and review steps from FileFast Glob",
    "content": "Identify the relevant goods or services, tax period and applicable refund restrictions. Reconcile input tax credit, output turnover and tax rates to invoices and returns. Check exclusions, formula inputs and current portal instructions before preparing a claim. Have unusual classifications or rate questions reviewed separately.\n\n## 1. Start with the facts\n\nConfirm the legal entity, tax registration, relevant period, transaction type and business location. The correct treatment can change with the facts, the applicable financial or assessment year and current portal instructions. Do not rely on a generic checklist where the transaction has unusual features.\n\n## 2. Working records to collect\n\n- Purchase invoices\n\n- Sales invoices\n\n- HSN classification\n\n- GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B\n\n- GSTR-2B\n\n- ITC ledger\n\n- Refund computation\n\n## 3. Review workflow\n\n1. Establish a source-of-truth register and preserve the original exports or documents.\n\n2. Match each material transaction to its invoice, ledger entry, portal record or contract reference.\n\n3. Classify differences instead of netting them off. Record the amount, reason, evidence and action owner.\n\n4. Reconcile the final working to the relevant return, application or management report before approval.\n\n5. Save the submitted form, acknowledgement, payment evidence and review notes together.\n\n## 4. Common errors to avoid\n\n- Assuming every rate difference qualifies\n\n- using incorrect turnover figures\n\n- ignoring notified exclusions\n\n- failing to reconcile ITC and return values.\n\n## 5. Questions to resolve before filing or submission\n\n- Is the correct entity, registration and period being used?\n\n- Do the supporting documents agree with the figures and declarations?\n\n- Have exceptions, amendments and prior-period items been separately reviewed?\n\n- Have current official portal instructions and applicable law been checked?\n\n- Has the responsible taxpayer or authorised person approved the final information?\n\n## How FileFast Global can help\n\nFileFast Global can help organise the relevant records, prepare reconciliations and coordinate the agreed filing or compliance workflow. The scope, professional fee, statutory charges and client approval responsibilities should be confirmed before work begins. We do not guarantee government approval, refund, tax outcome or processing time.\n\n## Official verification\n\nCheck the latest instructions and portal guidance from the relevant authority for the period involved. For Indian GST matters, use https://www.gst.gov.in/ and https://cbic-gst.gov.in/. For income-tax matters, use https://www.incometax.gov.in/. For MCA matters, use https://www.mca.gov.in/. For overseas tax, verify with the relevant country's official tax authority.\n\nDisclaimer: General information only, not case-specific tax, legal or financial advice. Rules, thresholds, rates, forms and deadlines may change. Confirm the current position and obtain appropriate professional advice before acting."
